---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const pageTitle = "About myself";
---

<Layout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
  <section class="hero-section about-hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <h2 class="hero-greeting">Hi, I'm Ellie 🌸</h2>
      <p>
        Hi there — I’m <strong>Luisa (Ellie) Escobar-Robledo</strong>, a physician-turned-computational
        biologist fascinated by how living systems think, adapt, and communicate through rhythm
        and signal.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="marker-grid about-grid">
    <article class="about-card about-card--blue">
      <header class="about-card__header">
        <h3>Where I'm From</h3>
      </header>
      <div class="about-card__body">
        <p>
          I was born and raised in Medellín, Colombia, where I studied medicine before moving
          into the world of data science and, eventually, computational biology. I’m now a
          PhD student in the <strong>Joint Carnegie Mellon – University of Pittsburgh Program</strong>,
          where I work under <strong>Dr. Keisuke Ishihara</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="about-card about-card--pink">
      <header class="about-card__header">
        <h3>What I Do</h3>
      </header>
      <div class="about-card__body">
        <p>
          My work lives at the intersection of medicine, data science, and computational biology.
          I aim to understand the electrical activity of the heart to potentiate the diagnostic
          and prognostic accuracy of electrocardiograms. In my current project, I aim to develop
          <strong>high-throughput platforms to record cardiac electrical activity</strong> of cardiac organoids.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="about-card about-card--lilac">
      <header class="about-card__header">
        <h3>Before Pittsburgh</h3>
      </header>
      <div class="about-card__body">
        <p>
          I am a General Physician from <strong>Universidad CES</strong>, where I graduated in 2018.
          During and after my studies I worked under <strong>Dr. Antoni Bayés de Luna</strong> as a
          researcher in Barcelona studying electrocardiograms and the role of the
          <strong>P wave as a prognostic factor in cardiovascular disease</strong>. Along the way, I fell in love
          with the space where cardiology meets computation which led me to pursue a Master's degree
          in Data Science and Analytics at <strong>Universidad EAFIT</strong>. Before moving to Pittsburgh,
          I worked as a data scientist at <strong>Rappi</strong>, developing predictive models for estimated
          delivery times.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="about-card about-card--blue">
      <header class="about-card__header">
        <h3>Beyond the Bench</h3>
      </header>
      <div class="about-card__body">
        <p>
          Outside the lab, you’ll find me writing, tinkering with things that glow, or geeking out
          about science like it’s storytelling. I’m also an anime fan, guitar learner, and unwavering
          coffee devotee (Colombian, always ☕️).
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="about-card about-card--pink">
      <header class="about-card__header">
        <h3>Why This Site Exists</h3>
      </header>
      <div class="about-card__body">
        <p>
          This corner of the internet is where I archive my research, catalog the reflections that
          keep me grounded, and share the small discoveries that keep my heart (and code) alive.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>
</Layout>
